# SPEC-060 LongMemEval evaluation harness (COMP-014 / REQ-195).
# The harness downloads a third-party dataset and builds a throwaway agent
# workspace per question; none of that is repo content. Every pattern here is
# anchored (leading `/`) and none of them covers a source directory: git cannot
# re-include a file beneath an ignored directory, so a `!` negation could never
# rescue harness code that fell under one. That is why evaluations/ingest/ and
# evaluations/longmemeval/ are peers of these paths and never inside them.
/evaluations/longmemeval/data/
/evaluations/runs/
/evaluations/results/
# Traces and the audit chain the agent writes inside a run workspace.
/evaluations/**/traces/
/evaluations/**/.audit/
# Generated agent configs, named individually. A blanket `*.toml` would hide 41
# tracked files — every pyproject.toml and all five blueprint.toml. (It would
# not touch the config/*.toml.example templates, which end in `.example`.)
/evaluations/**/arcagent.toml
/evaluations/**/arcllm.toml
/evaluations/**/arcrun.toml
# Repo-root guards. `ArcAgent(cfg)` without an absolute `config_path` resolves
# the workspace, trace dir, audit chain and capability scan root against the
# process CWD — which is this repo root. These catch that leak even if the
# harness makes the mistake. Anchoring is load-bearing: an unanchored
# `capabilities/` would hide packages/arcagent/src/arcagent/builtins/capabilities/.
/workspace/
/traces/
/.audit/
/capabilities/
/arcagent.toml
/arcllm.toml
/arcrun.toml

# Poolside
.poolside/

# Deployment — keep cloud-specific configs and credentials private.
# The public repo carries only the main agent framework; deploy paths
# (parameters.json with SSH keys / Object IDs / domain config) live
# in operator-controlled forks.
deploy/aws/
deploy/azure/
deploy/lib/

# Architecture analysis artifacts. These are Claude Code system files, not
# published documentation — they live under .claude/architecture/ and the
# `**/.claude/` rule above already covers them. These patterns catch the
# copies that tooling still drops at a package root.
tech-debt.json
packages/**/tech-debt.json
